<td class="py-3 px-4 text-emerald-400">-15% to -22%</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 text-xs text-slate-300 space-y-1">
<div class="font-bold text-amber-400 uppercase font-mono">UL 508A Supplement SB Compliance Note:</div>
<p class="leading-relaxed">
Substitutions are engineered strictly within UL 508A Table SB4.1 component rules. High-fault ratings (65kA to 100kA SCCR) are preserved by coordinating upstream Class J or Class CC current-limiting branch fuses to eliminate panel rating bottlenecks.
</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<!-- Tier-2 Prime Contractor Subcontracting Guide -->
<section class="py-16 bg-[#0B1120] border-b border-slate-800" id="tier2-subcontracting">
<div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 space-y-10">
<div class="max-w-3xl space-y-2">
<span class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-emerald-400 uppercase tracking-widest">Procurement Compliance Briefing</span>
<h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-white uppercase tracking-tight">
            Tier-2 Prime Contractor Diversity Subcontracting Briefing (FAR 19.7)
          </h2>
<p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            Essential operational guidance for general contractors, electrical contractors, and prime EPC estimators bidding regional semiconductor, data center, and critical infrastructure projects.
          </p>
</div>
<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 text-xs sm:text-sm">
<div class="p-6 rounded-lg bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 space-y-3">
<div class="font-mono text-emerald-400 font-bold uppercase">Dollar-for-Dollar Credit</div>
<h3 class="text-base font-bold text-white uppercase">ESRS / eSRS Reporting</h3>
<p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
100% of subcontracts placed with Sawtooth Industrial Systems LLC qualify for Small Disadvantaged Business (SDB) and Minority Business Enterprise (MBE) credit on prime contractor Individual Subcontract Reports (ISR - SF 294) and Summary Subcontract Reports (SSR - SF 295).
</p>
</div>
<div class="p-6 rounded-lg bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 space-y-3">
<div class="font-mono text-cyan-400 font-bold uppercase">Non-Manufacturer Rule</div>
<h3 class="text-base font-bold text-white uppercase">13 CFR § 121.406 Compliance</h3>
<p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
Sawtooth operates with verified commercial distribution facilities and partner fabrication channels that satisfy federal value-added reseller criteria, ensuring full audit protection under prime federal compliance reviews.
</p>
</div>
<div class="p-6 rounded-lg bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 space-y-3">
<div class="font-mono text-amber-400 font-bold uppercase">Regional Megafab Alignment</div>
<h3 class="text-base font-bold text-white uppercase">Treasure Valley Proximity</h3>
<p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
Local headquarters in Boise (Executive Dr) enables immediate job-site coordination, same-day submittal turnaround, and local warehouse buffer stocking for the Micron Megafab and Meta Kuna expansion corridors.
</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<!-- Electrical Formulas Reference -->
<section class="py-16 bg-[#0F172A] border-b border-slate-800">
<div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 space-y-8">
<div class="max-w-3xl space-y-2">
<span class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-cyan-400 uppercase tracking-widest">Electrical Formulas</span>
<h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-white uppercase tracking-tight">
            Three-Phase FLA &amp; Conductor Sizing Formulas
          </h2>
<p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            Standard engineering reference formulas utilized during panel submittal drafting.
          </p>
</div>
<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 font-mono text-xs">
<div class="p-6 rounded-lg bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 space-y-2">
<div class="text-amber-400 font-bold uppercase">Three-Phase FLA Formula</div>
<div class="text-white text-base font-bold py-2">I = P / (√3 × V × PF)</div>
<p class="text-slate-400">Where P is power in Watts, V is line-to-line voltage (e.g. 480V), and PF is operating power factor.</p>
</div>
<div class="p-6 rounded-lg bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 space-y-2">
<div class="text-cyan-400 font-bold uppercase">Motor Branch Circuit Sizing</div>
<div class="text-white text-base font-bold py-2">Ampacity ≥ 125% × FLA</div>
<p class="text-slate-400">Per NEC Article 430.22, conductors supplying a single motor must have an ampacity rating ≥ 125% of motor full-load current.</p>
</div>
<div class="p-6 rounded-lg bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 space-y-2">
<div class="text-emerald-400 font-bold uppercase">Heat Dissipation (Watts to BTU)</div>
<div class="text-white text-base font-bold py-2">BTU/hr = Watts × 3.412</div>
<p class="text-slate-400">Converts total internal electrical losses into required refrigeration cooling capacity.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>


</BaseLayout>
